    "created_at": "2026-03-31T10:00:25Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-03-31T10:00:25Z",
    "body": "> I agree we should, but as far as I can tell that would not solve this problem. This happens as part of processing the \"template\" start tag which is not an element.\n\nRight, it still needs a special case, but at least there is some concept of this being a \"template\" at this stage so it can feel a bit more natural than reverse-engineering a `ShadowRoot` inside a `DocumentFragment` into a template with attributes (or delaying transforming the template into a `ShadowRoot`).",
